This software uses FFmpeg and FFprobe as separate bundled programs.

FFmpeg is licensed under the GNU Lesser General Public License (LGPL)
version 2.1 or later. Some redistributed Windows and Linux builds are
upgraded to LGPLv3 because they enable `--enable-version3` for
LGPL-compatible libraries that require it (for example Apache 2.0
components). Those builds still do not enable `--enable-gpl` or
`--enable-nonfree`.

Video Lab launches FFmpeg and FFprobe as external processes. It does not
link against libavcodec, libavformat, or other FFmpeg libraries.

Copyright notices and the full license texts are included in this directory.

FFmpeg source code:
https://github.com/FFmpeg/FFmpeg

macOS binaries are compiled from the official FFmpeg n8.1 source without
`--enable-gpl` and without `--enable-nonfree`.

Windows and Linux binaries come from BtbN FFmpeg-Builds, `lgpl` variant:
https://github.com/BtbN/FFmpeg-Builds
